-- name: Verify passed but no test touched alongside source
-- class: Consistency
-- metric: alignment_collect_d2
-- action: add or update tests alongside the source changes that shipped, or fix the project's verify command if it does not actually exercise tests
-- severity: WARN
-- guardrail: BOTH SIDES OF THIS DISAGREEMENT LIVE IN alignment-collect's OWN d2 RECORD -- spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-loopsmith-insight-data-platform-design.md:529's own parenthetical names alignment-collect d2 tests_touched_with_source_pct directly; alignment-collect.sh's own printf (lines 448-449) emits tests_touched_with_source_pct and test_command_known together in one object, so no join is needed or possible. POPULATION IS SCOPED TO PACKS THAT ACTUALLY CARRY A d2 BLOCK (json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2') IS NOT NULL), NOT MERELY THE RIGHT schema -- a bare schema = 'alignment-collect/v1' filter (coverage_gate_absent.sql's own shape, this rule's first draft) was proven live to be a false-PASS trap (.sdlc/plans/120.md Design decision 2 / Key facts item 3): a store whose packs exist but never populated d2 at all reads a non-zero population under that scoping while test_command_known IS TRUE can never match against a NULL, rendering a confident false PASS for a dimension that was never measured; scoping to "d2 is present" instead renders the honest ABSENT. FIRES ONLY ON ZERO TOUCHED TESTS (tests_touched_with_source_pct = 0), NEVER A PERCENTAGE CUTOFF -- an existence/emptiness comparison against 0, matching coverage_gate_absent.sql's/coverage_degraded_collector.sql's own established idiom, deliberately not a tuned magnitude. REQUIRES commits_with_source > 0 SO A TRIVIAL 0% IS NEVER MISREAD AS A REAL DISAGREEMENT -- alignment-collect.sh only computes tests_pct nonzero when COMMITS_WITH_SOURCE > 0 (line 396); a window with zero source commits emits tests_touched_with_source_pct: 0 trivially, and this rule must not fire on that. test_command_known IS TRUE, NEVER IS NOT FALSE -- a payload missing the key entirely reads NULL, and NULL IS TRUE is FALSE, correctly excluding it from evidence (three-valued logic, Design decision 5); NOTE FOR A FUTURE READER: a d2 record that is present (passes this rule's own population scoping) but omits test_command_known entirely therefore renders PASS, not ABSENT, at this rule's own grain -- unreachable through the real alignment-collect.sh writer today (it always emits test_command_known whenever it emits d2 at all, per its own printf line 448), but a future, less disciplined writer of a d2-shaped payload that copies this population-scoping idiom without also always supplying test_command_known would see that gap silently. MALFORMED-PAYLOAD DISCLOSURE (systemic, pre-existing, not fixed here): a fact_collector_pack row whose schema = 'alignment-collect/v1' and whose raw_payload is non-NULL but not valid JSON makes every json_extract call in this rule's population and evidence queries raise DuckDB's InvalidInputException, crashing evaluate_rule rather than degrading to ABSENT -- the identical, unguarded json_extract(raw_payload, ...) pattern every one of the six already-shipped rules (and metrics 5/20/24/41) already shares. This fails LOUD, not silent, so it is not a false PASS and is not spec:534's forbidden collapse; widening scope to guard every json_extract call across the catalog against a malformed payload is out of this story's scope (see .sdlc/plans/120.md Risks).
-- population: SELECT count(*) FROM fact_collector_pack WHERE schema = 'alignment-collect/v1' AND json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2') IS NOT NULL
SELECT
    project_id,
    collected_ts,
    CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') AS INTEGER) AS commits_with_source,
    CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.tests_touched_with_source_pct') AS INTEGER) AS tests_touched_with_source_pct,
    CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.test_command_known') AS BOOLEAN) AS test_command_known
FROM fact_collector_pack
WHERE schema = 'alignment-collect/v1'
  AND CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.test_command_known') AS BOOLEAN) IS TRUE
  AND COALESCE(CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') AS INTEGER), 0) > 0
  AND CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.tests_touched_with_source_pct') AS INTEGER) = 0
ORDER BY project_id, collected_ts
